# BeHazeld Windows Self-Hosting Environment Guide

This setup removes Railway, Neon, Cloudinary, and Vercel from the live system.

Final domains:

- Storefront: `https://www.behazeld.com`
- Admin OS: `https://admin.behazeld.com`
- Backend API: `https://api.behazeld.com`

Windows server IP:

- `54.224.2.26`

## 1. Backend `.env`

Create this file on the Windows server:

`C:\BeHazeld\The-Complete-Story\BeHazeld_OS_Backend\.env`

Use:

```env
APP_ENV=production
APP_NAME=BeHazeld E-Commerce OS
API_V1_PREFIX=/api/v1
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://behazeld_app:CHANGE_THIS_PASSWORD@127.0.0.1:5432/behazeld_os
JWT_SECRET_KEY=CHANGE_THIS_TO_A_LONG_RANDOM_BACKEND_SECRET
JWT_ALGORITHM=HS256
ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRE_MINUTES=30
REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRE_DAYS=7
UPLOAD_STORAGE_PROVIDER=local
UPLOAD_LOCAL_PATH=C:\BeHazeld\data\uploads
PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://api.behazeld.com
INVOICE_STORAGE_PATH=C:\BeHazeld\data\invoices
MAX_REQUEST_BODY_BYTES=10485760
ALLOWED_ORIGINS_RAW=https://www.behazeld.com,https://behazeld.com,https://admin.behazeld.com,http://127.0.0.1:3000,http://127.0.0.1:3001
```

## 2. Storefront `.env.local`

Create/update this file:

`C:\BeHazeld\The-Complete-Story\BeHazeld_Website\frontend\.env.local`

Use:

```env
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://api.behazeld.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_TENANT_ID=b86e1ba8-2d77-4eed-a069-4041504d3717
ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET=CHANGE_THIS_TO_A_LONG_RANDOM_STOREFRONT_SECRET
ADMIN_API_KEY=Gappu@2023
```

## 3. Admin `.env.local`

Create this file:

`C:\BeHazeld\The-Complete-Story\BeHazeld_OS_Admin\.env.local`

Use:

```env
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.behazeld.com
```

## 4. Local Folders

Create these folders on Windows:

```powershell
mkdir C:\BeHazeld\data
mkdir C:\BeHazeld\data\uploads
mkdir C:\BeHazeld\data\invoices
mkdir C:\BeHazeld\logs
```

## 5. DNS Records

Create these DNS records where the domain was purchased:

```text
Type: A
Name: www
Value: 54.224.2.26

Type: A
Name: admin
Value: 54.224.2.26

Type: A
Name: api
Value: 54.224.2.26
```

Optional root domain:

```text
Type: A
Name: @
Value: 54.224.2.26
```

## 6. Ports

Internal app ports:

- Backend FastAPI: `127.0.0.1:8000`
- Storefront Next.js: `127.0.0.1:3000`
- Admin Next.js: `127.0.0.1:3001`

Public ports:

- HTTP: `80`
- HTTPS: `443`

